A||||8||SCCA FIERO||New Project: TURBO FORMULA
Z||000000||SCCA FIERO||08-07-99||07:31 PM||||I finished putting the V6 in my 88 coupe and installed the factory spoiler from my old 86SE. I also got a set(and 2 extras) of 87GT wheels and painted the insides black. I have what appears to be a Formula. I also put a 120mph speedo and shortened shifter in the cockpit. That is pretty much done....getting bored now.<p>MY NEXT PROJECT: FORCED INDUCTION.<br>Today I went to the junkyard and pulled the turbo off of an 87 Turbo T-Bird. This turbo is water-cooled and has a huge radiator type of houseing the compressed air travels through before it goes in the intake. The inter-cooler(air type) is pretty big and I am not sure it will fit, but I am gonna try. I will get an MSD boost master and ingition to control detonation and then get my Y-pipe fabricated. It looks like the turbo will fit, but will be a tight squeeze.
Z||000001||Cooter||08-07-99||08:56 PM||||Sounds like a fun project. But I have one question- How will you provide the extra enrichment required when running under boost? I have read that the stock electronics cant keep up past about three pounds of boost.
Z||000002||SCCA FIERO||08-07-99||09:05 PM||||The MSD boost and ignition will keep everything working right. I have to get a programed chip to provide the extra fuel needed or an rising rate fuel pressure regulator.
Z||000003||lowCG||08-07-99||09:12 PM||||Don't a few companies(Paxton does I know)sell fuel pressure regulators that raise the pressure under boost,and are adjustable?<br>You accesories will need a check valve(brake booster,and every other vacume-thing).<br>You will have fun with all that stuff,I'm sure,could go with an old Trans Am hood scoop to fit the intercooler?<br>Did you ever get that fender boxed up? :)<br>My friends are joking that you could just put a bunch of stamps on it,cram it into a mailbox,since it's dent resistant urethane.LOL<br>
Z||000004||SCCA FIERO||08-07-99||09:23 PM||||LOL...I will get that thing to ya soon I hope. I also need to send a sail-panel to Bayboy. I just keep forgetting bout it. Batboy if you read this send me your address again. 
Z||000005||terryk||08-08-99||11:06 AM||||A friend and I are in the middle of this project. We are using a 280 Z blower (rebuilt) and a Syclone/Sunbird ECM (1227749) since it has wastegate control, supports 2 BAR map, ESC sensor. Some code changes are needed, but that's not a big deal. We expect to have to go to 30lb-ish injectors. The stock Fiero's are 16lb. <p>The 85 6869 ECM supports turbo, but needs the wastegate quad driver circuit (not populated on the 6869) and a new chip. The 7170 had the turbo code completely removed.<p>The 7749 comes out to be a better solution.<p>You can run the un-modified 6869 into the couple-pound range. You wouldn't want to go over about 5-6 PSI without a knock sensor and 8.9:1 compression. That's pushing it.<p>For those wanting more compression on an NA engine 3.1L, you can mill the heads about .030" and bring the compression up to a bit over 9.1:1. The intake should be milled to match the drop in head height. Don't go more than that. The water jackets get too thin. A partner milled his .060". It works, but the intake sits on the block and front and rear sealing is not great.
Z||000006||SCCA FIERO||08-15-99||02:33 AM||||(Just keeping my thread alive til I get more done)<br> <br>I pulled my oilpan to install the drain fitting from the turbo and change the leaking gasket.<p>terryk, what kind of injectors you using?
Z||000007||terryk||08-15-99||12:59 PM||||Either Vette 22 lbs or Buck SC 30 lbs injectors. The problems is that when you go to bigger injectors, they get hard to control at low pulse widths. You wind up having to mess with the low pulse width tables.<p>We'll make the final decision when we see what the O2 reads at WOT.<p>
Z||000008||SCCA FIERO||08-15-99||09:58 PM||||Will the stock injectors keep up with a turbo? <p>I am trying to make sure I get the right fitting in my oilpan. I will need to get a hose made for the oil return from the turbo to the pan and I am not sure what kind of fittings and threads would be used on the hose. See my problem? Anyone know about hoses? Anyone know what "NPT" means? I think it means National Pipe Thread. Where can I find this type of threaded fitting? I have gone to Home Depot and ACE and I think I have the correct fitting but not sure.
